@@ -0,0 +1,72 @@
+@logic
+Feature: Todo Filtering
+  As a user
+  I want to filter the todo list by completion status
+  So that I can focus on active or completed tasks
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded fresh
+
+  Scenario: Default route shows all todos
+    Given the application starts at the "#/" route
+    And the following todos exist:
+      | title    | completed |
+      | Buy milk | false     |
+      | Learn JS | true      |
+    Then all todos are visible in the list
+
+  Scenario: Active filter shows only active todos
+    Given the following todos exist:
+      | title    | completed |
+      | Buy milk | false     |
+      | Learn JS | true      |
+    When the user clicks the "Active" filter link
+    Then the "Active" filter link has class "selected"
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is visible in the list
+    And the todo "Learn JS" is not visible in the list
+    And the URL hash is "#/active"
+
+  Scenario: Completed filter shows only completed todos
+    Given the following todos exist:
+      | title    | completed |
+      | Buy milk | false     |
+      | Learn JS | true      |
+    When the user clicks the "Completed" filter link
+    Then the "Completed" filter link has class "selected"
+    And the todo "Learn JS" is visible in the list
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is not visible in the list
+    And the URL hash is "#/completed"
+
+  Scenario: Filter persists on reload with route change
+    Given the following todos exist:
+      | title    | completed |
+      | Buy milk | false     |
+      | Learn JS | true      |
+    When the user clicks the "Active" filter link
+    And the app is reloaded
+    Then the "Active" filter link has class "selected"
+    And the todo "Buy milk" is visible in the list
+    And the todo "Learn JS" is not visible in the list
+
+  Scenario: Item hidden by filter when its state changes
+    Given the following todos exist:
+      | title    | completed |
+      | Buy milk | false     |
+    When the user clicks the "Active" filter link
+    And the user clicks the toggle checkbox on "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" is not visible in the list
+
+  Scenario: All filter link is default selected
+    Given the application starts at the "#/" route
+    Then the "All" filter link has class "selected"
+
+  Scenario: Browser back button restores previous filter
+    Given the following todos exist:
+      | title    | completed |
+      | Buy milk | false     |
+      | Learn JS | true      |
+    When the user clicks the "Completed" filter link
+    And the user clicks the "All" filter link
+    And the user navigates back in browser history
+    Then the "Completed" filter link has class "selected"
+    And the todo "Learn JS" is visible in the list
\ No newline at end of file
