@@ -0,0 +1,114 @@
+@logic
+Feature: Todo Management
+  As a user
+  I want to add, complete, and remove todos
+  So that I can track my tasks
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded fresh
+
+  Scenario: App starts with no todos
+    Then "#main" is hidden
+    And "#footer" is hidden
+    And the todo list is empty
+    And the todo-count shows "0 items left"
+
+  Scenario: User adds a todo
+    When the user types "Buy milk" into the new-todo input and presses Enter
+    Then a new todo appears in the list with title "Buy milk"
+    And the new-todo input is cleared
+    And "#main" is visible
+    And "#footer" is visible
+    And the todo-count shows "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: User trims whitespace from new todo
+    When the user types "   Learn TodoMVC   " into the new-todo input and presses Enter
+    Then a new todo appears in the list with title "Learn TodoMVC"
+
+  Scenario: User cannot add an empty todo
+    When the user types "" into the new-todo input and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list remains empty
+
+  Scenario: User completes a todo
+    Given the following todos exist:
+      | title    |
+      | Buy milk |
+    When the user clicks the toggle checkbox on "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" has class "completed"
+    And the todo-count shows "0 items left"
+
+  Scenario: User uncompletes a todo
+    Given the following todos exist:
+      | title    | completed |
+      | Buy milk | true      |
+    When the user clicks the toggle checkbox on "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" does not have class "completed"
+    And the todo-count shows "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: User removes a todo with the destroy button
+    Given the following todos exist:
+      | title    |
+      | Buy milk |
+      | Learn JS |
+    When the user clicks the destroy button on "Buy milk"
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" is not in the list
+    And the todo "Learn JS" remains in the list
+    And the todo-count shows "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Mark all as complete toggles all todos
+    Given the following todos exist:
+      | title    |
+      | Buy milk |
+      | Learn JS |
+    When the user clicks the toggle-all checkbox
+    Then all todos have class "completed"
+    And the toggle-all checkbox is checked
+    And the todo-count shows "0 items left"
+
+  Scenario: Mark all as complete unchecks when a single todo is unchecked
+    Given the following todos exist:
+      | title    | completed |
+      | Buy milk | true      |
+      | Learn JS | true      |
+    When the user clicks the toggle checkbox on "Buy milk"
+    Then the toggle-all checkbox is not checked
+
+  Scenario: Mark all as complete checkbox is checked when all todos completed
+    Given the following todos exist:
+      | title    | completed |
+      | Buy milk | true      |
+      | Learn JS | true      |
+    Then the toggle-all checkbox is checked
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed removes all completed todos
+    Given the following todos exist:
+      | title      | completed |
+      | Buy milk   | true      |
+      | Learn JS   | false     |
+      | Write code | true      |
+    When the user clicks the "Clear completed" button
+    Then the todo "Buy milk" is not in the list
+    And the todo "Write code" is not in the list
+    And the todo "Learn JS" remains in the list
+    And the todo-count shows "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed button is hidden when no completed todos
+    Given the following todos exist:
+      | title    |
+      | Learn JS |
+    Then the clear-completed button is hidden
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed button is visible when completed todos exist
+    Given the following todos exist:
+      | title    | completed |
+      | Learn JS | true      |
+    Then the clear-completed button is visible
+
+  Scenario: Counter pluralizes correctly
+    Given the following todos exist:
+      | title      | completed |
+      | Task one   | false     |
+      | Task two   | false     |
+      | Task three | true      |
+    When the user views the todo-count
+    Then the count reads "2 items left"
